title: The Democratic Conference
subtitle: Coalition or a socialist government?
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: dix >= 18
priority: 25
max-visits: 1

= The Democratic Conference

Between 27 September and 5 October, 1,500 delegates from the soviets, the unions, the cooperatives, the zemstvos and the dumas met at the Alexandrinsky Theatre. The conference was convened by the Soviet executive to decide the future of the government. It ended in a muddle: the delegates voted for a coalition, then voted against coalition with the Kadets, then voted for the original formula with the Kadets, in a form that Kerensky later called a joke.

[? if player_party = 'menshevik' : The party's two leaders disagree. Tsereteli wants a coalition, with the Kadets, on the grounds that without the propertied classes, Russia will not be governed. Dan wants a homogeneous socialist government. ?][? if player_party = 'sr' : The party disagrees with itself. The Right SRs want a coalition, with the Kadets, on the grounds that without the propertied classes, Russia will not be governed. Chernov's Centre and the Left SRs want a government of the socialist parties alone. The conference elects Avksentiev, one of your own, to chair the Pre-Parliament that it creates. ?]In the corridors, Trotsky sits and watches.

- @coalition: Back coalition with the liberals, as before.
- @socialist: Force a homogeneous socialist government.
- @pre: Take seats in the Pre-Parliament, as a loyal opposition.
- @lsr_boycott: Walk out with the Bolsheviks, and boycott the Pre-Parliament.

@coalition
view-if: player_party != 'lsr'
on-arrival: {!
Q.in_coalition = 1;
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 3, 0);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', -2, 8);
RO.add(Q, {rel_kad: 4, rel_ally: -2, bolshevik: 3});
!}

The Conference declared for coalition. [+ Dlbl +] are satisfied. Kerensky's cabinet is nonetheless the same.

@socialist
choose-if: rel_ally >= 55
unavailable-subtitle: The SRs will not support this.
on-arrival: {!
Q.in_coalition = 1;
Q.gov_kadets = 0;
Q.homogeneous_gov = 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_kad: -10, right_threat: 4, bolshevik: -3, soviet_democracy: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', -3, 10);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 3, -5);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 10);
!}

The Menshevik Defencists and Internationalists have, for once, agreed. A government of the Soviet parties, without the liberals, will be formed.

@pre
view-if: player_party != 'lsr'
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {rel_kad: 2, soviet_democracy: -1});
RO.boost(Q, {middle: 1, workers: -1});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 2, 0);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 4);
!}

We entered the Pre-Parliament, which is a body of advice without a mandate, to be elected by nobody. The Bolsheviks walked out, loudly.

@lsr_boycott
view-if: player_party = 'lsr'
on-arrival: {!
Q.lsr_backs_bol = 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: 6, rel_ally: -6, soviet_democracy: -1});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 2, workers: 1, peasants: 1});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 3, -2);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 8);
!}

The Left SR delegates left the hall with the Bolsheviks, and said that the Pre-Parliament was a body without a mandate. The SR leaders say that the Left has chosen its allies.
